{"id": "en_story_chile_miners", "tag": "TRUE STORY", "cta": "MORE TRUE STORIES LIKE THIS", "ctaSmall": "follow", "ctaWhere": "new story every day", "accent": "#FF8C42", "lang": "en", "total": 71.75, "segments": [{"text": "On 5 August 2010 a catastrophic copper and gold mine collapse traps 33 workers underground.", "start": 0.0, "end": 5.96}, {"text": "The San Jose mine in Chile caves in, burying the men roughly 700 meters deep.", "start": 6.34, "end": 10.2}, {"text": "For 17 agonizing days the entire world has zero idea if anyone survived this disaster.", "start": 10.78, "end": 15.74}, {"text": "Down in a cramped underground refuge the trapped miners desperately ration tiny amounts of food.", "start": 16.42, "end": 20.68}, {"text": "They survive on spoonfuls of canned tuna and sips of dirty water while waiting.", "start": 21.14, "end": 24.78}, {"text": "Above ground rescue teams drill narrow holes into the black rock searching for life.", "start": 25.36, "end": 29.06}, {"text": "On day 17 a drill finally breaks through the darkness and pulls back up.", "start": 29.06, "end": 32.82}, {"text": "Attached to the metal drill bit is a handwritten note written in red ink.", "start": 33.24, "end": 36.12}, {"text": "It reads Estamos bien en el refugio los 33 which means We are well in the shelter.", "start": 36.58, "end": 41.36}, {"text": "Relief sweeps across Chile and the world as everyone learns the miners are alive.", "start": 41.9, "end": 45.8}, {"text": "Engineers quickly build a narrow metal rescue capsule specifically named Fenix 2.", "start": 46.34, "end": 49.876}, {"text": "On 13 October 2010 all 33 men are hoisted safely to the surface one by one.", "start": 50.42, "end": 54.9}, {"text": "They spend a staggering 69 total days trapped in the dark before seeing sunlight.", "start": 54.9, "end": 59.36}, {"text": "This incredible rescue captivates millions of people watching every single second live on television.", "start": 59.84, "end": 64.44}, {"text": "Could you s